' ============================================================
' FirstProgram.dbas — Your first DBasic program
' ============================================================
' This program asks for your name, makes it ALL CAPS using a
' Go standard-library package, then prints a greeting using a
' SUB defined in another DBasic file.
'
' Two ways DBasic pulls in code from outside this file:
'   1. IMPORT  — borrows a Go package (here: "strings")
'   2. INCLUDE — pastes another .dbas file in (here: greeter.dbas)
' ============================================================

' Borrow Go's "strings" package. Now we can call strings.ToUpper.
IMPORT "strings"

' Pull in our helper file. The SUB SayHello defined there
' becomes usable below.
INCLUDE "greeter.dbas"

SUB Main()
    ' DIM creates a labeled box that holds text (a STRING).
    DIM name AS STRING

    ' Ask the user a question. The semicolon at the end keeps
    ' the cursor on the same line so they can type their answer.
    PRINT "What is your name? ";
    INPUT name

    ' Use Go's strings.ToUpper to convert "alice" into "ALICE".
    DIM shouty AS STRING = strings.ToUpper(name)

    ' Call the SUB from greeter.dbas.
    SayHello(shouty)
END SUB
